From: SoundTap <noreply@soundtap.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] watchdog: omap_wdt: keep the timer running through a restart

omap_wdt's shutdown hook disables the hardware watchdog whenever it is in
use, and device_shutdown() runs it on every reboot. Whatever comes after
it -- the shutdown of the devices registered before the watchdog, and the
PRM warm reset itself -- then runs with no watchdog at all. A stall there
leaves the speaker without network or USB until someone pulls the plug
(a rollout hang). Leave the timer running on a restart; on
power-off and halt it is still stopped. A reset that does happen clears
the timer with everything else.
---
--- a/drivers/watchdog/omap_wdt.c	2026-10-26 05:33:24.526958258 +0100
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/omap_wdt.c	2026-10-26 05:33:31.214931192 +0100
@@ -298,6 +298,15 @@
 {
 	struct omap_wdt_dev *wdev = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 
+	/*
+	 * Keep counting through a restart. Everything after device_shutdown() --
+	 * the remaining driver shutdowns and the PRM reset itself -- is otherwise
+	 * unguarded, and a stall there leaves the board dead until power is cut.
+	 * If the reset happens, the timer goes with it.
+	 */
+	if (system_state == SYSTEM_RESTART)
+		return;
+
 	mutex_lock(&wdev->lock);
 	if (wdev->omap_wdt_users) {
 		omap_wdt_disable(wdev);
